# Competency question: "What projection loss occurs when this statistical result is exported
# to RDF Data Cube?" The projection-side loss ledger made queryable for the Data-Cube target:
# a math:ProjectionRecord projects a math: statistical result (math:projectionSource) into the
# RDF Data Cube (math:projectionTargetName), declares its preservation polarity
# (logic:preservationKind — SoundUnderApproximation: the cube is sound but incomplete), and
# enumerates EACH construct it cannot carry (logic:unsupportedConstruct), reusing the logic:
# loss-ledger vocabulary verbatim (Principle 17). The query returns one row per dropped
# construct — model assumptions, inference method, distribution parameterization, and
# proof/provenance — so "what is lost, and is the loss recorded" is answerable rather than
# silent. The target is projected as its string form (STR(...)) so its cell is a plain
# literal. Scoped to the fixture namespace so the answer is exactly the Data-Cube export's
# recorded drops.
PREFIX math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>

SELECT ?projection ?target ?preservation ?dropped WHERE {
    ?projection a math:ProjectionRecord ;
                math:projectionSource ?source ;
                math:projectionTargetName ?targetRaw ;
                logic:preservationKind ?preservation ;
                logic:unsupportedConstruct ?dropped .
    BIND(STR(?targetRaw) AS ?target)
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?projection), "http://example.org/math/"))
}
ORDER BY ?projection ?dropped
